<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Illinois Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1832 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An alliance of Algonquian peoples of the upper Mississippi valley, close partners of the French, whose name lives on in the state of Illinois.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, or Inoka, were a group of a dozen or more related peoples, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaskaskia">Kaskaskia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoria">Peoria</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/cahokia">Cahokia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamaroa">Tamaroa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michigamea">Michigamea</a>, who lived along the Illinois and middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> rivers by the 17th century. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-marquette">Jacques Marquette</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-jolliet">Louis Jolliet</a> visited in 1673, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-village-of-the-illinois">Grand Village</a> of the Kaskaskia near Starved Rock held thousands of people.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Each tribe had its own village chiefs, with war and peace chiefs, and the confederation shared language, ceremonies and alliances. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and hunted bison on the prairies in seasonal expeditions. Allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-france">New France</a>, they hosted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missions and French settlements such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaskaskia">Kaskaskia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/cahokia">Cahokia</a>, and many became Catholic. Iroquois attacks in 1680 and wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meskwaki">Fox</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sauk">Sauk</a> and others reduced their numbers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Epidemics, alcohol and war shrank the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> from perhaps 10,000 to a few hundred by 1800. After the killing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawa">Ottawa</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pontiac">Pontiac</a> by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoria">Peoria</a> in 1769, enemies attacked them. They ceded their lands in treaties ending in 1832 and moved west; descendants form the Peoria Tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/illinois-confederation.jpg" alt="Illinois Confederation" width="229" height="337"><figcaption>Image: General Georges-Henri-Victor Collot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaskaskia_Illinois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1832 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Algonquian traditional religion, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Miami-Illinois</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Illiniwek, Illinois Confederacy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1716&amp;focus=illinois-confederation" aria-label="Illinois Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2258 768 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Illinois Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2578 1024h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2578 1024h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United States. <a href="/atlas?year=1716&amp;focus=illinois-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

